    title: "Morning update",
    summary: "Morning update Good Morning Middle East Eye readers, If you are just joining us, here are key developments from across the region and beyond: *Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps says its forces attacked two US bases in Bahrain; Manama says strikes hit civilian industrial facility. *The Saudi-led coalition said it intercepted and destroyed a ballistic missile launched by Yemen's Houthis towards Saudi Arabia's western region. *Two Palestinians injured in an Israeli strike on Gaza succumb as territory's health ministry says death toll since the October 2025 “ceasefire” rises to 1,661. *Israeli settlers torched Palestinian-owned vehicles and spray-painted alleged racist graffiti on Palestinian homes in several West Bank villages. *The Hind Rajab Foundation (HRF) has urged Germany to arrest an Israeli soldier, Almog Keisi, who has been sighted in Luneburg this week, accusing him of war crimes, crimes against humanity and acts of genocide in Gaza. *Turkish Foreign Minister Hakan Fidan has said Israel is blocking thousands of container homes destined for Gaza, adding that Israeli authorities argue Hamas could use the metal structures for manufacturing weapons. *Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian has said that his country was engaged in a \"silent war that is far more difficult than the one in which missiles are launched and destruction is inflicted\". *Lebanese President Joseph Aoun has accused Iran of meddling in Lebanon's affairs through Hezbollah's weapons and also demanded Israel withdraw from the country's south. *Pro-Israel US Democratic leader, Hakeem Jeffries has pledged to advance legislation targeting Israeli settler violence in the occupied West Bank within the first 100 days of the new Congress.",
